// LZ78 - Hello World! :: RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   colour     : not assigned by Linguist
//   layer      : full (byte-balanced rainbow bar)
//   upstream   : https://github.com/quxianp/RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   reference  : see https://esolangs.org/ and https://rosettacode.org/

# LZ78 over "Hello World!". Each phrase added to the dictionary emits
# an index into it, the length of the phrase, and the one new character
# the phrase extends -- which is what distinguishes it from LZ77's
# distance/length pairs.
#   index  72  length 1  then +'e'
#   index 101  length 1  then +'l'
#   index 108  length 1  then +'l'
#   index 108  length 1  then +'o'
#   index 111  length 1  then +' '
#   index  32  length 1  then +'W'
#   index  87  length 1  then +'o'
#   index 111  length 1  then +'r'
#   index 114  length 1  then +'l'
#   index 108  length 1  then +'d'
#   index 100  length 1  then +'!'
#   index  33  length 1  then (end of input)
